{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1280,
    "dDurationMs": 1810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The universe is expanding."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3090,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you zoom out far enough, you’ll find\nthat everywhere in the universe is moving"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6000,
    "dDurationMs": 1750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "away from everywhere else."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7750,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But once you know the universe is expanding,\nyou might wonder if it’s going to keep expanding"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11550,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "somehow, or eventually stop and crunch in\non itself because of the attractive force"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15240,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of gravity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16240,
    "dDurationMs": 3610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, all you have to do is point your telescope\nat a distant galaxy, measure how fast it’s"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19850,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "moving away from us, wait about a million\nyears, and then do the same thing again to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23530,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "see if the galaxy is moving faster or slower\nthan before."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26950,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if you don’t have a million years to\nspare, here’s what you do."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30130,
    "dDurationMs": 2120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You look at different galaxies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32250,
    "dDurationMs": 3620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because light takes time to reach us, when\nwe look at a galaxy far, far away, we see"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35870,
    "dDurationMs": 2050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it as it was a long time ago."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37920,
    "dDurationMs": 4439,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So looking at a bunch of galaxies different\ndistances away is kind of a rough proxy for"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42359,
    "dDurationMs": 2731,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "looking at the same one at different times."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45090,
    "dDurationMs": 3969,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The light from the stars in a distant galaxy\ncan tell us two basic things."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49059,
    "dDurationMs": 4831,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First, its speed: light from anything moving\naway from you becomes redder in color (kinda"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53890,
    "dDurationMs": 3179,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like how police sirens get lower in pitch\nwhen moving away)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57069,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This redshifting of light tells us exactly\nhow fast stars are moving away from us."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61269,
    "dDurationMs": 3941,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If the light from a star is 5 percent redder\nthan it should be, it means the star is moving"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65210,
    "dDurationMs": 2519,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "away from us at 5 percent the speed of light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67729,
    "dDurationMs": 4430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Light can also tell us how far away a star\n(and thus its parent galaxy) is."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72159,
    "dDurationMs": 3181,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When you’re driving at night, you can tell\nhow far away a motorcycle is by comparing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75340,
    "dDurationMs": 3529,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how bright its headlight seems to you, to\nhow bright it would be if you were right in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78869,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "front of it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79869,
    "dDurationMs": 1460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The same trick works with stars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81329,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There’s a rare kind of supernova explosion\nthat’s like a standard interstellar headlight"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85289,
    "dDurationMs": 4281,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "– it’s about 5 billion times brighter\nthan our sun, and, crucially, it’s very"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 89570,
    "dDurationMs": 1799,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "consistent in its brightness."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91369,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These only happen a few times in a galaxy\nevery thousand years, but there are enough"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 95969,
    "dDurationMs": 4091,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "galaxies in the universe that, if you look\nclosely at a wide enough patch of sky, it’s"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100060,
    "dDurationMs": 2660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "possible to see a dozen of them go off in\na month."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 102720,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By comparing the brightness as seen here on\nEarth with how bright we know each of them"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 106140,
    "dDurationMs": 3380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "should be, we can work out how far away each\nsupernova is."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109520,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The dimmer its light, the farther away it\nis."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111710,
    "dDurationMs": 4630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the color of a type Ia supernova tells\nus how fast it’s moving away from us, and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116340,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "its brightness is like a ruler, telling us\nhow far away it is – or, because light takes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120700,
    "dDurationMs": 3349,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "time to get here, how long ago we’re measuring\nits speed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 124049,
    "dDurationMs": 3981,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By measuring the speed of different supernovae\nat different distances – aka different"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128030,
    "dDurationMs": 3860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "times in the past – we can plot the expansion\nof the universe over time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 131890,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A straight line means the universe is expanding\nat a constant rate, a curve means it’s speeding"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 136370,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "up or slowing down."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 137870,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For a long time we thought the line was straight,\nor slightly curved in the slowing down direction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 142170,
    "dDurationMs": 4959,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But when astronomers finally looked carefully\nat supernova in super-distant galaxies, they"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 147129,
    "dDurationMs": 5411,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "discovered, to their surprise, that the universe\nis expanding faster now than it was long ago."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 152540,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The universe’s expansion is accelerating!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 155780,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "p.s."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 157380,
    "dDurationMs": 3689,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We have a few basic ideas for why the universe\nis accelerating, but we still don’t really"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 161069,
    "dDurationMs": 1471,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "know why it’s happening."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 162540,
    "dDurationMs": 3770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One of the simplest and most popular ideas\nis that there’s an everywhere-permeating"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 166310,
    "dDurationMs": 3950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "vacuum energy with negative pressure which\nwe’ve never detected in any way other than"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 170260,
    "dDurationMs": 2050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by measuring the expansion of the universe..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 172310,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so we call it dark energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 175030,
    "dDurationMs": 4510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thanks to the Wide Field Infrared Survey Telescope\nproject at NASA Goddard Space Flight Center"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 179540,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the Space Telescope Science Institute\nfor supporting this video."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 182720,
    "dDurationMs": 4340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "WFIRST is planned to launch in the mid-2020s,\nand will, among other things, allow us to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 187060,
    "dDurationMs": 4940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "see a much wider swath of the sky at Hubble-like\nresolutions and even farther distances, and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 192000,
    "dDurationMs": 2930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thus hunt for more supernovas many billions\nof light years away."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 194930,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That’ll help us understand whether the acceleration\nof the universe is different in different"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 198470,
    "dDurationMs": 3719,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "parts of the universe or whether it has changed\nover time, which should help us figure out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 202189,
    "dDurationMs": 2621,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what exactly dark energy is."
    } ]
  } ]
}
